---
import Layout from './Layout.astro';
import SearchWorkbench from './SearchWorkbench.astro';
const base = '/raveldex/';
---
<Layout wide frontmatter={{ title: 'Search the usage guides' }}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={base + 'demo/ui.css'} />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={base + 'site-assets/workbench.css'} />
    <script is:inline type="module" src={base + 'demo/main.mjs'}></script>
  </Fragment>
  <header class="search-home__intro">
    <h1>Try search on the usage guides</h1>
    <p>Search, filter and open a guide. Explore how the results change.</p>
  </header>
  <SearchWorkbench advanced />
  <section class="search-home__example site-main--article" aria-labelledby="demo-keyboard">
    <h2 id="demo-keyboard">Use the controls</h2>
    <p>Press Tab to move between controls and result links, or Return to submit from the search field. Choose a Document category to narrow matches and All to clear it. Changing page shows more results without changing the total. These updates keep focus on the control you used.</p>
    <p>Open Inspect results to see which terms matched and how scores were calculated. Close Inspector or press Escape to return focus to that button. Snippets are short excerpts; follow a result link to read the complete guide.</p>
    <p>Try <code>source provide</code> to complete the final word, or <code>unmatchedword</code> for an empty result. Choose a sample query to recover. Advanced demo settings let you compare final-word prefix, exact-word and strict adjacent phrase searches, source reanalysis, stored positions, direct execution and one module worker.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="search-home__follow" aria-labelledby="demo-copy">
    <div><h2 id="demo-copy">Add search to your application</h2>
      <div class="search-home__links"><a href={base + 'reference/hosts/#mount-a-minimal-search-form'}>UI integration example <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href={base + 'guide/overview/'}>Getting started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      <p>The <a href={base + 'example-files/ui.mjs'}>ui.mjs example</a> creates an engine, adds one document and supplies its display title and URL. Follow the setup instructions before running it.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="search-home__code"><figcaption>JavaScript · From an initialized engine</figcaption><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Search code example"><code>const result = await engine.search('module worker');</code></pre></figure>
  </section>
</Layout>
